[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2438544553","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98529#issuecomment-2438544553","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98529","id":2438544553,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RWTyp","user":{"login":"zeux","id":1106629,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDY2Mjk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1106629?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux","html_url":"https://github.com/zeux","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-25T18:23:39Z","updated_at":"2024-10-25T18:34:43Z","body":"For posterity, summary of future work that I think would be valuable; I want to try to get to some of this this year but no promises...\r\n\r\n- Remove now-unused raycast mode as we discussed before to simplify (ha!) the code\r\n- Restructure LOD generation flow to have finite LOD-dependent error limits and remove the patch to switch to combined distance+attribute error (this will produce different LOD switch distances but in general should result in much fewer LOD switches that visibly degrade quality)\r\n- Adjust LOD generation to use previous LOD for next LOD as a source (significantly improving import performance in the process)\r\n- Change the default normal merge limit as 60 degrees is too high to generate good normals in some cases, as the simplifier is being fed a model with bad normals to begin with\r\n- Enable PRUNE mode, probably unconditionally (it was designed to just work), to improve quality/size balance further on complex models\r\n- Incorporate bone influence information into the attributes that the simplifier sees to improve behavior under  deformation","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2438544553/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2438546840","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98529#issuecomment-2438546840","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98529","id":2438546840,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RWUWY","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-25T18:25:12Z","updated_at":"2024-10-25T18:25:12Z","body":"Curious question, does this pr resolve the outstanding issues with animation bone weights?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2438546840/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2438549671","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98529#issuecomment-2438549671","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98529","id":2438549671,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RWVCn","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-25T18:27:06Z","updated_at":"2024-10-25T18:28:02Z","body":"> This also may require changing the default normal merge limit - Godot currently uses 60 degree cutoff to merge normal vertices, which is really not great for normal quality on meshes with creases.\r\n\r\nSee also https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/94108 where the merge angle is currently hardcoded to 60 degrees (matching the 3D scene import default). It could be exposed as an option still.\r\n\r\nWhat would be a more reasonable default? Intuitively, I would say either 45 degrees or even 44 degrees (to keep 45-degree angles intact).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2438549671/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2438552046","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98529#issuecomment-2438552046","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98529","id":2438552046,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RWVnu","user":{"login":"zeux","id":1106629,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDY2Mjk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1106629?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux","html_url":"https://github.com/zeux","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-25T18:28:42Z","updated_at":"2024-10-25T18:30:59Z","body":"> does this pr resolve the outstanding issues with animation bone weights\r\n\r\nNo - as the simplifier is not aware of the bone influences, it will not make different decisions. Ideally, fixing that issue is predicated on a) use of combined distance+attribute metric (see above), b) actually giving simplifier some sort of bone influence data like we discussed.\r\n\r\nWithout (b), the simplifier is still going to collapse side edges of a cylinder as it just doesn't know anything about bone structure. With (b), it will be able to produce intermediate LOD levels that preserve this deformation, but crucially all of them will have very small positional error (and high attribute error!), so unless the renderer uses the combined error, the LOD switches will still break the mesh visually under deformation.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2438552046/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2438555193","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98529#issuecomment-2438555193","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98529","id":2438555193,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RWWY5","user":{"login":"zeux","id":1106629,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDY2Mjk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1106629?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux","html_url":"https://github.com/zeux","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-25T18:30:47Z","updated_at":"2024-10-25T18:30:47Z","body":"> What would be a more reasonable default? Intuitively, I would say either 45 degrees or even 44 degrees (to keep 45-degree angles intact).\r\n\r\nYeah I was thinking something like 30-40 degrees but this would need to be experimented with.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2438555193/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2440370625","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98529#issuecomment-2440370625","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98529","id":2440370625,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RdRnB","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-28T02:09:56Z","updated_at":"2024-10-28T02:09:56Z","body":"Thank you!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2440370625/reactions","total_count":